WEBVTT

NOTE
Journey: Advocates - Week 13 Student Video
Unit 4, Lesson 1: Morality

1
00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:29.460
Can you be good without God? Do you need to believe in God to know morality?

2
00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:35.020
Does the existence of a moral law point towards a moral law giver?

3
00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:38.140
Or can morality be explained by evolution?

4
00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:43.440
These are some of the most common and yet important questions we can ask.

5
00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:48.860
In Romans chapter 2, the Apostle Paul says that even people without the law

6
00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:53.080
know right and wrong because it's written on their hearts.

7
00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:58.440
In other words, part of being human is that we know there's a moral law.

8
00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:04.060
In fact, we know it so clearly, says Paul, that God can judge us based upon it.

9
00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:08.040
So in Romans chapter 1, Paul says that creation points towards a creator.

10
00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:12.780
And now in Romans chapter 2, he says the existence of a moral law that we know

11
00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:15.880
clearly points towards a moral law giver.

12
00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:18.940
Let's take a minute and flesh this out.

13
00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:24.380
When developed, this is referred to as the moral argument for the existence of God.

14
00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:27.520
Now keep something in mind before we look at the particulars.

15
00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:30.940
We're not saying that people have to believe in God to be moral.

16
00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:35.100
We're not saying that people have to believe in God to know right from wrong.

17
00:01:35.540 --> 00:01:38.100
Atheists can be moral. Pantheists can be moral.

18
00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:43.480
Christians can be immoral. But we are arguing that if there is an objective moral

19
00:01:43.480 --> 00:01:46.060
standard then there must be a God.

20
00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:50.180
Think about it. You can read a book if you don't believe in authors.

21
00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:53.380
All you need to do is know how to read.

22
00:01:53.660 --> 00:01:58.720
But the question is, can there be things such as books if there's not authors?

23
00:01:58.940 --> 00:02:01.160
And the answer to that is obviously no.

24
00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:05.880
Similarly, people can be moral if they don't believe in God.

25
00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:07.960
That's not the interesting question.

26
00:02:08.180 --> 00:02:13.380
The question is, can there be a real right and wrong objective morality if there is

27
00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:17.000
no God? The answer to that is no. In

28
00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:32.500
his classic novel, The Brothers Karamazov, Russian novelist Fyodor Dostoevsky famously

29
00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:38.460
said if there is no God all is permissible in other words if there's not

30
00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:44.360
a transcendent moral source outside of human beings then well anything goes

31
00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:50.420
the late atheist philosopher Friedrich Nietzsche said if there is no God then it's

32
00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:53.120
those with power who get to determine right and wrong.

33
00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:58.720
In other words, if God doesn't exist, then it's those with the biggest guns who get

34
00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:00.020
to determine morality.

35
00:03:01.460 --> 00:03:06.260
So here's the moral argument for the existence of God stated more formally.

36
00:03:06.460 --> 00:03:08.600
It has two premises and a conclusion.

37
00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:14.760
The first premise is if there are objective moral values and duties, then God

38
00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:20.620
must exist. So what is it about morality that points towards God well for one

39
00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:24.920
moral values and duties aren't physical you can't weigh them they don't have

40
00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:29.720
extension in space they can't be studied by science moral values and duties contain

41
00:03:29.720 --> 00:03:35.560
information commands about how we are supposed to live they point towards a source

42
00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:41.380
outside of mankind instructing us about how we're supposed to behave there's something

43
00:03:41.380 --> 00:03:46.100
about moral values and duties that has a spiritual core the

44
00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:51.460
second premise is that objective moral values and duties exist

45
00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:57.040
now how can I make such a claim well two reasons for one in his classic book The

46
00:03:57.040 --> 00:04:02.100
Abolition of Man C.S. Lewis famously pointed out that across cultures throughout the

47
00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:07.820
history of the world there's a commitment to certain universal moral principles

48
00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:13.620
that justice is better than injustice that courage is good that we ought to care

49
00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:19.080
for our children and our posterity now as Lewis points out how we practice those

50
00:04:19.080 --> 00:04:24.640
moral principles might vary across culture but there is a universal agreement and

51
00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:30.500
commitment to the underlying moral principles second people simply

52
00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:35.760
know that there's a right and wrong we all live as if we believe

53
00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:40.900
morality is objective. My dad often has said to me, he said, son, you know

54
00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:42.300
what people believe about right and wrong?

55
00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:47.280
Not by what they say, not by what they do, but by how they want to be

56
00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:53.160
treated. Everybody wants to be treated as if promise keeping is an objective feature

57
00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:57.820
of the universe. So I often tell my students, if someone says to you, there's no

58
00:04:57.820 --> 00:05:00.580
such thing as objective morality, cut in front of them in line.

59
00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:02.860
And what are they going to say? That's not fair.

60
00:05:02.980 --> 00:05:07.300
That's not right, as if there's a moral standard that we're all supposed to

61
00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:07.540
follow.

62
00:05:08.860 --> 00:05:13.420
A few years ago I sponsored a public debate with three of my high school students

63
00:05:13.420 --> 00:05:18.800
and three students from the public school free-thinking atheist agnostic club.

64
00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:23.220
They debated the historical Jesus, intelligent design, and morality.

65
00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:28.220
One of my students got up there and said there is an objective moral law, we know

66
00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:31.360
it. Therefore, there's a moral law giver.

67
00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:35.780
Morality points towards God. Then one of their students got up there and said, there

68
00:05:35.780 --> 00:05:39.640
is no objective moral law. In fact, morality is all subjective.

69
00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:41.660
It's like picking an ice cream flavor.

70
00:05:41.880 --> 00:05:45.660
You have your moral truth and I have mine and we all live accordingly.

71
00:05:45.980 --> 00:05:50.400
And then he sat down. Then when it was time for the concluding speech, instead of

72
00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:55.580
summarizing why he thinks that their team won, one of the free thinking students got

73
00:05:55.580 --> 00:06:00.380
up there and this is what he said he said you Christians are bigoted hateful and

74
00:06:00.380 --> 00:06:05.900
intolerant shame on you for the way that you live I sat there and I thought wait a

75
00:06:05.900 --> 00:06:10.740
minute just moments before he said morality is subjective it's entirely

76
00:06:10.740 --> 00:06:16.740
individualistic and there's no objective standard then he got up there and he says

77
00:06:16.740 --> 00:06:22.740
you Christians have violated every single moral norm shame on you, you

78
00:06:22.740 --> 00:06:27.700
should have known differently. You see his worldview said there's no such thing as

79
00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:32.380
objective moral values and duties but he couldn't live it out consistently.

80
00:06:33.460 --> 00:06:38.820
Simply put this argument shows that the best explanation for the existence of

81
00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:43.320
objective moral values and duties is that there is a personal God.

82
00:06:43.640 --> 00:06:46.660
Now this alone doesn't prove that the Christian God exists.

83
00:06:46.980 --> 00:06:52.660
It raises challenges for both pantheism and naturalism, but broadly speaking it's

84
00:06:52.660 --> 00:06:55.380
consistent with a God of Judaism and a God of Islam.

85
00:06:55.800 --> 00:07:00.520
What this argument shows is that the physical world is not all that exists.

86
00:07:00.760 --> 00:07:03.140
There is a spiritual and a moral realm.

87
00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:06.320
There is a God who cares about the way that we live.

88
00:07:06.500 --> 00:07:10.080
There is a God who will hold us accountable for how we live our lives.

